[1mOne real bug found and fixed.[22m The C [38;5;10mparse_val[0m does [38;5;10merrno = 0;[0m and then [38;5;10mstrtol[0m, which sets [38;5;10mERANGE[0m on [38;5;10mlong[0m overflow. The Rust translation reimplemented [38;5;10mstrtol[0m by hand and never touched [38;5;10merrno[0m, so after a call an external caller saw stale or wrong [38;5;10merrno[0m — differing both on success (C leaves 0, Rust left the previous value) and on overflow inputs like [38;5;10m"9223372036854775808"[0m (C leaves 34, Rust left 0). I added an [38;5;10merrno[0m shim in [38;5;10msrc/lib.rs[0m and made [38;5;10mparse_val[0m clear it up front and set [38;5;10mERANGE[0m when the emulated conversion overflows. The printed output was already correct in every case; only this side channel diverged.[0m[0m
